==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|rectifier||to make straight}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|rēctificāre||make right}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|rēctus||straight}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛktəˌfaɪ/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|rectif|ies}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[correct]] or [[amend]] something.
# {{lb|en|transitive|chemistry}} To [[purify]] or [[refine]], especially by [[distillation]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|electronics}} To [[convert]] [[alternating current]] into [[direct current]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To produce (as factitious gin or brandy) by redistilling bad wines or strong spirits (whisky, rum, etc.) with flavourings.
# {{lb|en|transitive|geodesy}} To adjust (a globe) in order to prepare for the solution of a proposed problem.

